// t_472ff302: an unknown identifier in type position must be REFUSED, and the
// compiler must terminate.  Before the fix this source made rsx-cg-compiler
// spin for ever - not slowly, never - and it did so under --dump-ast too,
// because the parse loop never reached a back end.
//
// The cause was not this type: Parser::error() records a diagnostic without
// consuming a token or throwing, so a declaration that failed left the cursor
// where it was and the top-level loop called it again on the same token.  Any
// failure that neither advances nor throws did this.  'bogusType' is simply
// the shortest way to reach it.
//
// 95 shaders in the reference SDK sample tree never terminated, most of them
// over the Cg 1.x type name texobj2D - which is a REAL type the reference
// accepts, and supporting it is a separate row.  This fixture only asks that
// an unknown one be refused rather than hung on.
void main(uniform bogusType t, float4 c : TEXCOORD0, out float4 o : COLOR)
{
    o = c;
}
